# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in what you have.
#
# DATABASE_URL and AUTH_SECRET are REQUIRED — the app fails clearly on
# startup/first request without them (see lib/db/client.ts,
# DatabaseNotConfiguredError). Everything else degrades gracefully:
# every tool that needs a credential reports itself as NOT CONNECTED
# (with the real reason) until it's set, rather than faking a result.

# --- Database (required) ---------------------------------------------
# A real PostgreSQL connection string. Locally: any Postgres (see
# migrations/ + `pnpm migrate`). In production: a Neon database
# (Vercel's native Postgres integration) or any other Postgres
# provider's connection string. Never exposed to the browser — read
# only in lib/db/client.ts (server-only).
DATABASE_URL=

# --- Auth (required) --------------------------------------------------
# Auth.js's session-signing secret. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Never reuse this between environments; never commit it.
AUTH_SECRET=

# --- Google OAuth (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Enables "Continue with Google" on the login and signup screens. The
# button ONLY appears when BOTH of these are set (see isGoogleConfigured
# in lib/auth.ts) — if either is missing, Google sign-in is silently
# not registered and the UI shows email + password only. No fake OAuth.
# Create credentials at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# and add this authorized redirect URI:
#   <your-origin>/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Password reset delivery (optional) ------------------------------
# Password reset generates a real single-use, 1-hour token and stores
# only its SHA-256 hash (see app/api/auth/forgot-password). There is no
# email provider wired up, so outside production the reset link is
# returned to the browser and shown directly (clearly labeled) rather
# than pretending an email was sent. To deliver real emails, add an
# email provider (e.g. Resend) and send the link from that route.

# --- Runtime mode -------------------------------------------------------
# Set to true ONLY in local/preview development to route every LLM call
# through the deterministic local fixture instead of a real provider —
# see lib/agent/tools/llm-providers/development.ts. Hard-blocked when
# VERCEL_ENV=production regardless of this value (lib/runtime-mode.ts)
# — a real deployment can never accidentally serve simulated results.
LLM_DEV_MODE=

# Which LLM provider the worker's LLM tool actually calls. Defaults to
# anthropic. An unrecognized value is treated as NOT CONFIGURED (with
# the exact bad value named) — it never silently falls back to a
# different provider's credentials.
LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic

# --- Anthropic (Messages API) ---------------------------------------
# Required by THREE things, only one of which depends on LLM_PROVIDER:
#
#   1. Workforce's LLM tool and every skill built on it (Trend
#      Research and the rest) — when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic. Without
#      the key they block with "Configure ANTHROPIC_API_KEY".
#   2. Knowledge → AI Summary (lib/knowledge/ai-summary.ts).
#   3. Knowledge → Ask / grounded answering (lib/knowledge/answer.ts,
#      POST /api/knowledge/ai). Without the key the endpoint returns
#      503 and the UI says Ask is not configured — it never answers
#      from the model's own memory.
#
# (2) and (3) are pinned to Anthropic and do NOT follow LLM_PROVIDER:
# their configuration checks, their 503s and their user-facing copy
# all name this variable, so following a deployment-wide provider
# switch would make them report a credential state unrelated to what
# they actually called.
#
# All three reach the provider through lib/ai/llm (shared platform).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the model used for real analysis (defaults to
# claude-sonnet-5, confirmed current for this deployment).
LLM_MODEL=

# Optional: override the Anthropic API base URL (defaults to
# https://api.anthropic.com). Deliberately a different variable name
# than ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, which some environments reserve for their
# own tooling.
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL_PUBLIC=

# --- Gemini (Generative Language API) --------------------------------
# ONE credential, TWO independent features. Read this before assuming
# which one you have configured:
#
#   1. TEXT GENERATION — needs GEMINI_API_KEY + GEMINI_MODEL, and only
#      applies when LLM_PROVIDER=gemini.
#   2. EMBEDDINGS / SEMANTIC SEARCH — needs GEMINI_API_KEY +
#      GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL, and applies REGARDLESS of LLM_PROVIDER.
#      Knowledge uses Gemini for embeddings even when answers are
#      generated by Anthropic.
#
# The key is shared; the two model variables are not interchangeable
# and neither implies the other. Setting GEMINI_API_KEY alone enables
# nothing.

# Shared by both features above.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Gemini: text generation -----------------------------------------
# Required when LLM_PROVIDER=gemini. There is no built-in default (no
# model id written here can be confirmed current), so a missing value
# is treated exactly like a missing credential. Set it to a currently
# supported gemini-* model id, e.g. one listed at
# https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models at the time you deploy.
# NOT used for embeddings.
GEMINI_MODEL=

# --- Gemini: embeddings (Knowledge semantic search) ------------------
# REQUIRED for semantic search over the Knowledge library. Without it
# (or without GEMINI_API_KEY) retrieval silently degrades to lexical
# only: exact word matching with AND semantics and no stemming, which
# answers far fewer natural-language questions. The degradation is
# reported, never hidden — see docs/knowledge-semantic-search.md and
# the `executed.semantic` field on every search result.
#
# Requirements for the model you choose:
#   * it must support the `outputDimensionality` parameter. The
#     earlier `models/embedding-001` explicitly does NOT and will not
#     work here.
#   * the pipeline requests outputDimensionality=768 and REFUSES any
#     other width before writing to the database, because storage is
#     migrations/0008's `vector(768)` with an HNSW cosine index.
#
# As with GEMINI_MODEL, no default is provided and no model id is
# guessed. Pick a current embedding model from
# https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/embeddings at the time you
# deploy.
GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=

# Optional: override the Gemini API base URL (defaults to
# https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com). Used by both the
# generation and the embedding clients.
GEMINI_BASE_URL_PUBLIC=

# --- Cost ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: override the assumed $/1M-token pricing used to compute
# real AI cost from real token usage. Token counts always come from the
# active provider's own usage field — these only change the $/token
# assumption, never what's real. LLM_INPUT/OUTPUT_COST_PER_MTOK apply to
# Anthropic (kept as the original, provider-agnostic names for
# backward compatibility) and default to Sonnet-class list pricing.
# Gemini has no built-in default rate — set GEMINI_INPUT_COST_PER_MTOK /
# GEMINI_OUTPUT_COST_PER_MTOK explicitly, or its real cost is reported
# as unavailable rather than guessed.
LLM_INPUT_COST_PER_MTOK=
LLM_OUTPUT_COST_PER_MTOK=
GEMINI_INPUT_COST_PER_MTOK=
GEMINI_OUTPUT_COST_PER_MTOK=

# --- Search / Tools -------------------------------------------------------
# Two search tools exist, and a Worker gets whichever one is registered
# on it — no skill branches on which is configured.
#
#   tool_web_search    lib/agent/tools/web-search.ts — the public npm
#                      registry. Keyless, and the one search-like host
#                      this environment's egress policy allowlists, so
#                      it stays the honest default.
#   tool_tavily_search lib/agent/tools/tavily-search.ts — the live web,
#                      via api.tavily.com. Needs the key below AND
#                      api.tavily.com reachable from the deployment.
#
# TAVILY_API_KEY is read server-side only, at call time, and is written
# into exactly one place: the Authorization header of the search
# request. It never reaches a URL, a log line, a result or an error
# message — see sanitizeProviderMessage() in that file. Leave it unset
# and the Tavily tool reports itself NOT CONFIGURED rather than
# failing mid-execution; skill_objective_research then blocks with that
# reason instead of answering without sources.
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# --- Trusted proxy hops ---------------------------------------------
# How many proxies sit in front of this application and are trusted to
# have appended to X-Forwarded-For.
#
# This decides the SUBJECT of every pre-session rate limit (password
# reset, password forgot, /api/knowledge/preview). The client IP is
# taken that many entries from the RIGHT of the header, because
# anything a client forges arrives at the LEFT.
#
#   unset / 1   one trusted proxy — correct on Vercel, and for the
#               ordinary single reverse proxy. This is the default.
#   2+          an extra CDN or load balancer in front of that one.
#   0           nothing in front is trusted, so X-Forwarded-For is
#               ignored entirely and every caller shares one bucket.
#               This is the honest setting for a deployment reached
#               directly (a bare `next start` with no proxy): it
#               degrades the limit instead of leaving a forgeable one.
#
# Getting this too HIGH is the dangerous direction — it walks left into
# entries a client controls. Too low only costs precision.
TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=

# --- Knowledge durable ingestion (cron worker) -----------------------
# Required for POST /api/knowledge/tick — the Commit 12B recovery
# worker that drains any Knowledge ingestion job left stranded because
# after()'s fast-path claim never ran (see that route's own header).
# Vercel calls a scheduled route (see vercel.json) with
# `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}`; this route rejects every
# request (401) whose header doesn't match, constant-time, including
# when this var is unset — there is no "open" fallback. Generate a
# real random value (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) for any deployment
# that enables the cron; never reuse a value from another project.
CRON_SECRET=
